    {
      "id": "c4-l2",
      "title": "else if, && and ||",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "A chain of else if checks one condition after the other, and runs the first one that's true. The final else catches everything that's left.",
        "&& means and: both must be true. || means or: one is enough. ! means not: it turns true into false.",
        "C stops early: in a && b, if a is false, b isn't even looked at. Programmers use this a lot, like if (n != 0 && 10 / n > 2)."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "#include <stdio.h>",
          "",
          "int main() {",
          "    int score = 83;",
          "    if (score >= 90)",
          "        printf(\"A\\n\");",
          "    else if (score >= 80)",
          "        printf(\"B\\n\");",
          "    else if (score >= 70)",
          "        printf(\"C\\n\");",
          "    else",
          "        printf(\"F\\n\");",
          "    return 0;",
          "}"
        ],
        "output": [
          "B"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "c4-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "In the example, what does a score of 95 print?",
          "options": [
            "A",
            "A and B",
            "B",
            "F"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The first true condition wins, and the rest of the chain is skipped."
        },
        {
          "id": "c4-l2-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "When is a && b true?",
          "options": [
            "When both are true",
            "When at least one is true",
            "When both are false",
            "Always"
